      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-311206",
      ":question/problem": "$V = \u03c0 \\cdot 3r \\cdot r^{2}$\nA cylindrical can has a height that is $3$ times its radius $r$ of the base. The function $V$, given above, models the volume of the can, in cubic inches. Which expression represents the height, in inches, of the can?"
